1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:02,640
A good scam call doesn't sound like one.

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:05,240
It sounds polite. Even helpful.

3
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:10,040
In ScamSuno, every caller is fictional.

4
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:12,160
Not every caller is lying.

5
00:00:12,795 --> 00:00:17,610
Choose a language. We'll use English for
this offline, typed walkthrough.

6
00:00:19,595 --> 00:00:23,580
A fictional bank caller brings up a
service notice. What's it about?

7
00:00:26,145 --> 00:00:30,230
Type a question in your own words. We ask
what the notice is about.

8
00:00:33,595 --> 00:00:37,650
The caller describes a general update and
points us to the fictional app.

9
00:00:42,932 --> 00:00:46,767
Before acting on the call, open a channel
that you already trust.

10
00:00:50,492 --> 00:00:54,487
The fictional app confirms the notice. Who
called is still unverified.

11
00:00:55,942 --> 00:00:59,617
The debrief records our independent check
and safe exit.

12
00:01:01,062 --> 00:01:05,747
Gnani Prisma transcribes a short voice
turn. You review it before sending.

13
00:01:06,962 --> 00:01:09,987
The engine selects a reviewed response for
the scenario.

14
00:01:11,452 --> 00:01:14,467
Separate decision rules check what your
reply supports.

15
00:01:15,042 --> 00:01:19,277
Gnani Timbre reads the approved caller
line. Then it's your turn.

16
00:01:21,212 --> 00:01:25,787
What if the trusted app can't match the
notice? Here's a second offline call.

17
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:31,680
Nothing here is obviously wrong. That's
what makes it hard.

18
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:34,930
So you check somewhere the caller can't
control.

19
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:38,490
No matching notice.

20
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:42,020
Not proof of fraud, but not enough to
trust the call.

21
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:47,510
End the call to see what was really going
on,

22
00:01:47,550 --> 00:01:49,790
and which of your choices mattered.

23
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:53,380
Anything the call didn't test isn't
scored.

24
00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:57,110
Some calls are genuine. Some are scams.

25
00:01:57,150 --> 00:01:59,130
Some never become clear.

26
00:01:59,170 --> 00:02:04,460
ScamSuno. Practise on a call that doesn't
matter, before one that does.
